    "text": "{\nQuestion: \"When approaching a stop sign, what must you do?\"\nChoice 1: \"Slow down only if another car is coming\"\nChoice 2: \"Stop completely before proceeding\"\nChoice 3: \"Keep driving if the road looks clear\"\nChoice 4: \"Stop only if there is a police officer nearby\"\nAnswer: 2\n}\n\n{\nQuestion: \"What does a red traffic light mean?\"\nChoice 1: \"Slow down and continue\"\nChoice 2: \"Stop, then go if no one is coming\"\nChoice 3: \"Stop completely until the light turns green\"\nChoice 4: \"Speed up before the light changes\"\nAnswer: 3\n}\n\n{\nQuestion: \"What does a yellow traffic light mean?\"\nChoice 1: \"The light is about to turn red\"\nChoice 2: \"You must speed up\"\nChoice 3: \"You may ignore it\"\nChoice 4: \"The road is closed\"\nAnswer: 1\n}\n\n{\nQuestion: \"What should you do when an emergency vehicle with flashing lights or siren approaches?\"\nChoice 1: \"Stop in your lane immediately\"\nChoice 2: \"Speed up to get away\"\nChoice 3: \"Pull over to the right and stop if safe\"\nChoice 4: \"Follow the emergency vehicle closely\"\nAnswer: 3\n}\n\n{\nQuestion: \"What does a solid yellow line on your side of the road mean?\"\nChoice 1: \"Passing is allowed\"\nChoice 2: \"Passing is not allowed\"\nChoice 3: \"The road is one-way\"\nChoice 4: \"You must stop\"\nAnswer: 2\n}\n\n{\nQuestion: \"What does a broken yellow line mean?\"\nChoice 1: \"Passing may be allowed when safe\"\nChoice 2: \"Passing is never allowed\"\nChoice 3: \"Only trucks may pass\"\nChoice 4: \"The lane is ending\"\nAnswer: 1\n}\n\n{\nQuestion: \"What should you do before changing lanes?\"\nChoice 1: \"Only use your horn\"\nChoice 2: \"Signal, check mirrors, and check blind spots\"\nChoice 3: \"Move quickly without signaling\"\nChoice 4: \"Brake suddenly\"\nAnswer: 2\n}\n\n{\nQuestion: \"What is a blind spot?\"\nChoice 1: \"An area behind your car that mirrors may not show\"\nChoice 2: \"A place where traffic lights do not work\"\nChoice 3: \"A road with no streetlights\"\nChoice 4: \"A lane only for bicycles\"\nAnswer: 1\n}\n\n{\nQuestion: \"What should you do at a railroad crossing when the lights are flashing?\"\nChoice 1: \"Drive across quickly\"\nChoice 2: \"Stop and wait until it is safe to cross\"\nChoice 3: \"Stop only if you see a train\"\nChoice 4: \"Go around the gate if it is down\"\nAnswer: 2\n}\n\n{\nQuestion: \"What does a yield sign mean?\"\nChoice 1: \"You have the right-of-way\"\nChoice 2: \"Slow down and give the right-of-way if needed\"\nChoice 3: \"Stop for exactly five seconds\"\nChoice 4: \"The road is closed ahead\"\nAnswer: 2\n}\n\n{\nQuestion: \"At a four-way stop, who should go first?\"\nChoice 1: \"The driver who arrived first\"\nChoice 2: \"The largest vehicle\"\nChoice 3: \"The driver turning left\"\nChoice 4: \"The fastest driver\"\nAnswer: 1\n}\n\n{\nQuestion: \"If two vehicles arrive at a four-way stop at the same time, who should usually go first?\"\nChoice 1: \"The driver on the left\"\nChoice 2: \"The driver on the right\"\nChoice 3: \"The driver with the louder horn\"\nChoice 4: \"The driver who moves first\"\nAnswer: 2\n}\n\n{\nQuestion: \"What should you do when driving in heavy rain?\"\nChoice 1: \"Use high beams\"\nChoice 2: \"Drive faster to leave the rain\"\nChoice 3: \"Slow down and increase following distance\"\nChoice 4: \"Turn off your headlights\"\nAnswer: 3\n}\n\n{\nQuestion: \"What is hydroplaning?\"\nChoice 1: \"When tires lose contact with the road because of water\"\nChoice 2: \"When brakes become stronger in rain\"\nChoice 3: \"When the engine overheats\"\nChoice 4: \"When headlights reflect from snow\"\nAnswer: 1\n}\n\n{\nQuestion: \"What should you do if your vehicle starts to skid?\"\nChoice 1: \"Brake hard immediately\"\nChoice 2: \"Steer in the direction you want the vehicle to go\"\nChoice 3: \"Close your eyes briefly\"\nChoice 4: \"Turn the steering wheel sharply the opposite way\"\nAnswer: 2\n}\n\n{\nQuestion: \"When parking uphill with a curb, which way should you turn your front wheels?\"\nChoice 1: \"Toward the curb\"\nChoice 2: \"Away from the curb\"\nChoice 3: \"Straight ahead\"\nChoice 4: \"It does not matter\"\nAnswer: 2\n}\n\n{\nQuestion: \"When parking downhill with a curb, which way should you turn your front wheels?\"\nChoice 1: \"Away from the curb\"\nChoice 2: \"Toward the curb\"\nChoice 3: \"Straight ahead\"\nChoice 4: \"Toward the road\"\nAnswer: 2\n}\n\n{\nQuestion: \"What should you do before entering a highway from an entrance ramp?\"\nChoice 1: \"Stop at the end of the ramp\"\nChoice 2: \"Match the speed of traffic and merge when safe\"\nChoice 3: \"Force other drivers to slow down\"\nChoice 4: \"Drive on the shoulder\"\nAnswer: 2\n}\n\n{\nQuestion: \"What is the safest following distance in normal conditions?\"\nChoice 1: \"At least three seconds behind the vehicle ahead\"\nChoice 2: \"One foot behind the vehicle ahead\"\nChoice 3: \"Close enough to read the license plate\"\nChoice 4: \"Exactly one car length at any speed\"\nAnswer: 1\n}\n\n{\nQuestion: \"What should you do when following a motorcycle?\"\nChoice 1: \"Follow more closely because motorcycles are smaller\"\nChoice 2: \"Give extra following distance\"\nChoice 3: \"Drive beside it in the same lane\"\nChoice 4: \"Use your horn often\"\nAnswer: 2\n}\n\n{\nQuestion: \"What does a flashing red traffic signal mean?\"\nChoice 1: \"Slow down but do not stop\"\nChoice 2: \"Stop, then proceed when safe\"\nChoice 3: \"Speed up\"\nChoice 4: \"Only pedestrians must stop\"\nAnswer: 2\n}\n\n{\nQuestion: \"What does a flashing yellow traffic signal mean?\"\nChoice 1: \"Stop and wait for green\"\nChoice 2: \"Proceed with caution\"\nChoice 3: \"The road is closed\"\nChoice 4: \"You must turn left\"\nAnswer: 2\n}\n\n{\nQuestion: \"What should you do if a school bus stops with flashing red lights?\"\nChoice 1: \"Pass carefully on the left\"\nChoice 2: \"Stop and wait until the bus signals are off\"\nChoice 3: \"Pass if no children are visible\"\nChoice 4: \"Only slow down\"\nAnswer: 2\n}\n\n{\nQuestion: \"What should you do before making a right turn?\"\nChoice 1: \"Signal and move close to the right side of the road\"\nChoice 2: \"Move to the far-left lane\"\nChoice 3: \"Turn without slowing down\"\nChoice 4: \"Stop in the middle of the intersection\"\nAnswer: 1\n}\n\n{\nQuestion: \"What does a 'Slippery When Wet' sign warn drivers about?\"\nChoice 1: \"The road may be unusually slippery in wet weather\"\nChoice 2: \"The road is closed during rain\"\nChoice 3: \"Only trucks may use the road\"\nChoice 4: \"There is a gas station ahead\"\nAnswer: 1\n}\n"
